$image — text-to-image generation

SUMMARY
  Generates one or more PNG images from input prompts using a registered
  model (Flux + optional LoRA via fastimage). Supports multiple models and
  multiple variants per prompt.

SYNTAX
  $image(model='default')
  $image(model='crazy_desire')[2]
  $image(model=@image_models, seed=42, neg='blurry')

INPUT
  prompts[] — text prompts (newline-joined prompt link files). If empty,
              uses an empty string as one prompt.

OUTPUT
  images[] — new PNG links under op/images/
             Filenames: {YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS}_{model}_image_{i}.png
  texts[]  — when model_names_to_texts=True, one text link per image with
             the model name used for that image (same order as images[])

ARGUMENTS
  model=     — model name or @instruction (via arg_lists) for a list of
               models; each model runs over all prompts. Default: default
  model_names_to_texts= — when true/yes/1, append model name to texts[] for
               each generated image (one entry per image link)
  width= / height= — output size in pixels. If omitted, uses the model
               profile default (typically 768×512 for Flux). Both must be
               positive when set.
  count=     — variants per prompt (if [n] suffix not used)
  seed=      — base seed; per-prompt offset when seed > 0
  neg=       — negative prompt string

REPEAT SYNTAX
  $image(...)[n] — n output variants per prompt (same as count=n).

BEHAVIOR
  Loops: for each model × each prompt × count variants. One model load per
  model name. On ImportError / missing weights, falls back to emulated PNG
  placeholders unless AH_EMULATE_IMAGE is set.

DEPENDENCIES

  uv sync --extra image   (torch+cu128, bitsandbytes for NF4 Flux, diffusers, compel)

  Flux models (default, crazy_desire) do not need compel; compel is optional unless
  you use pony/sd1 profiles with use_compel.

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_IMAGE=1 — write placeholder PNGs without loading models.
  Models and LoRAs: externals/image/model_list.py, weights under models/.

EXAMPLE
  @images: @prompt -> $image(model='crazy_desire')[2]
  @images: @prompt -> $image(model='crazy_desire', width=1024, height=1024)[2]
  @images: @prompt -> $image(model=@image_models)[2]

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts[] cleared on output after the external returns.
